the latest on passengers from a carnival  cruise ship who are in quarantine in  seattle after a coveted outbreak  carnival won't say how many travelers  aboard the spirit were infected they  were moved into isolation in local  hotels after the ship docked in seattle  on tuesday this happened just days after  carnival reactivated its entire fleet  which had shut down when the pandemic  began nikki batiste has one of the  passenger's reaction  overwhelmed at sea that's how some  passengers aboard carnival spirit cruise  ship describe staff upon learning of a  covid outbreak i've been on seven  cruises since august  and of course covet is always a concern  darren seifertson was among those who  tested positive i literally stayed in  this room for six days  with no telephone service they wouldn't  answer the phone seifertson says his  travel companion and roommate stayed  with him in the room despite testing  negative and that a list of passengers  names and cabin numbers of those who had  contracted the virus was posted near  elevators the outbreak occurred during  the ship's voyage between miami where it  departed last month and seattle where it  arrived on tuesday upon docking all  infected passengers were moved to local  hotels for isolation carnival refused to  say how many of its approximately 2100  passengers tested positive but insists  travelers were vaccinated and tested  before boarding and in a statement to  cbs news said in part our health and  safety protocols exceed cdc guidelines  and additional measures were implemented  during the voyage but that brings little  comfort to passengers like seifertson  unfortunately this ship was so  unprepared  and so mismanaged  that many of us suffered greatly  for cbs mornings i'm nikki batiste  seven cruises since august that's a lot  of cruising
 

